  "title": "Taking a Well-Deserved Breather",
  "summary": "Even the most robust market rallies take pauses now and again. We got off to the now all-too-common “gentlemen, start your engines” move in the pre-market, but that failed to get sufficient follow-through after the opening burst. Since then, major US indices have meandered at roughly unchanged levels. It’s hardly a rout, but after a stretch that featured four straight 1% up moves in the Nasdaq 100 (NDX), today’s activity seems like an anticlimax.",
